ORA: Outspoken Revolutionary Art

We are a FLINTA*-made, queer collective of artists, dreamers & allies, created to amplify FLINTA* and queer voices in the artistic scene.

We move together, sharing what we know, what we’re learning, and what moves us.
From experienced hands to first steps, we grow in relation, not in hierarchy.

ORA grows from a shared desire
to support each other, to share, to explore, to love, and to dream together.

For our very first celebration on the 15.05.2026, we invite beautiful queer artists, DJs & performers to carry you through the night, from beginning to end.

Line up:
@gem.ini____
@oceane_cleopatre
@pegushaa
@saeed_sang.ab (performance)
@hannahwhitlow_ Glamanita (performance)

To make it truly alive, we need you.

Bring your wildest, softest, happiest energies, including the parts that feel heavy.
Your full presence, your truth, as you are.

We are back! This time on a Thursday night, going into May Day. Let’s go! xoxo

